sort command used to sort lines of text file 
 by default ascending Order

sort file alphabetically , numarically or in revers order 
to sort the lines aplphabetically 
#sort hello.txt 
Note: file will not modified 

when every you consider file is numbaric values , use below command 
Numarical sorting:
$sort -n file.txt 

how to sort reverse order 
#sort -r file.txt 
sort this data based on column 
#sort -k 3 file.txt

how to eliminate duplicate after sort 
#sort -u file.txt 
write a shell script to delete duplicate reocrds 
#!/bin/bash 
echo -n "enter filename :"
read fname 
sort -u $fname > tmp 
mv tmp $fname 
echo "duplicate records deleted form $fname "
